course: dictionary
lesson: 11046
title: Two meanings of one word
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. Webbing is one of these words. Read the words around it and ask: is this about a material, or about skin?
explain: «A pelican has four toes on each foot, all joined by webbing.» Here webbing is the skin that joins the toes. Pelicans use these big webbed feet to swim and to take off from the water.
explain: A nylon webbing strap on a bag is a different meaning. There, webbing is strong, flat woven material in narrow strips. Check each meaning by swapping it into the sentence: a strip joining the toes makes no sense, but skin joining the toes does.
fact: Webbing means strong, flat woven material in narrow strips, used for straps, belts, seat belts and bags.
fact: Webbing also means the skin between the toes of animals like ducks and frogs.
fact: «A pelican has four toes on each foot, all joined by webbing» shows the skin meaning.
fact: Phrases to know: nylon webbing, webbing strap, the webbing between its toes.
fact: When a word has two meanings, put each one into the sentence and see which one still makes sense.
exercise: «A pelican has four toes on each foot, all joined by webbing.» What is webbing in this sentence? | *The skin between the toes | Strong material for a bag | A kind of bird | Water that splashes
exercise: Mia's school bag has a webbing strap over her shoulder. What is the webbing? | A thin sheet of glass | *A strong, flat woven strip | A small toe | Wet feathers
exercise: Which of these animals has webbing between its toes? | Tiger | *Frog | Rabbit | Mouse
test: «A duck has three webbed toes and one free toe.» What does webbed mean here? | Very fast | Covered in woven straps | Made of nylon | *Having skin joining the toes
test: Which phrase uses webbing to mean strong, flat material? | The webbing between its toes | Webbed wings | A webbed foot | *Nylon webbing
exam: «Pelicans take off by running along the water, slapping these big feet.» Does webbing mean skin or material in the sentence that includes «all joined by webbing»? | Material for straps | *Skin between the toes | Material for belts | Skin
